/// Carrier trait — see `transport_serialization_design.md` §6.
///
/// A closed, tag-keyed trait: its implementations are the language's carriers, one per carrier
/// tag such as `(:tcp)`, `(:uart1)` or `(:ble_gatt)`, written in the compiler's tree for hosted
/// carriers and in a port's board tree for hardware carriers, and listed in the target's transport
/// pack. A program names a tag; it cannot implement one (E2409). The four properties are what the
/// framing layer needs; the carrier itself is an actor the program talks to with the messages of
/// design §6.2. No carrier exists yet: this file fixes the trait for the phases that add them.

export trait Carrier;
export mtu/1;
export boundaries/1;
export delivery/1;
export addressing/1;

required {
    fn mtu(c: Carrier) -> uint64;
    fn boundaries(c: Carrier) -> atom;
    fn delivery(c: Carrier) -> atom;
    fn addressing(c: Carrier) -> atom;
}
